amadeos-sample-books: public-domain classics for amadeOS
Source: https://github.com/datazuul/amadeos-sample-books

The books (/usr/share/amadeos/books)
------------------------------------
The texts are in the public domain: every author died before 1955, so they are free in the
European Union (70 years after the author's death) and in the United States (published before 1930).
books.tsv in this folder lists every book with its source.

- Books from Standard Ebooks (https://standardebooks.org): the editions, including their markup,
  covers and notes, are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal by Standard Ebooks.
- Books from Project Gutenberg (https://www.gutenberg.org): each book carries the Project Gutenberg
  License in its text. The books are given away free of charge, as that licence allows; the name
  "Project Gutenberg" is a trademark of the Project Gutenberg Literary Archive Foundation.

